          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Now I understand the full picture. Let me trace the zed agent's hook flow:\n\nThe zed agent's `install-hooks` installs a post-commit hook that calls:\n```\n$ENTIRE_CMD hooks zed session-start\n$ENTIRE_CMD hooks zed turn-start\n$ENTIRE_CMD hooks zed turn-end\n$ENTIRE_CMD hooks zed turn-start\n```\n\nWhen `entire hooks zed session-start` runs:\n1. `newHooksCmd` RunE fallback → `external.DiscoverAndRegister(discoveryCtx)` → discovers `entire-agent-zed` on PATH → registers it.\n2. `agent.Get(\"zed\")` succeeds.\n3. `executeAgentHook` → `handler.ParseHookEvent(ctx, \"session-start\", stdin)` → calls the zed binary's `parse-hook --hook session-start`.\n\nLet me look at the zed agent's `handleParseHook` to see what it returns.",
