          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Objective\n- Diagnose and fix why `entire` CLI 0.9.0 does not recognize the `entire-agent-zed` plugin: `entire agent add zed` errors with `unknown agent \"zed\"`, and `entire agent list` does not show Zed even after `entire enable --agent zed` installs hooks.\n- Verify the zed-agent git hook fires correctly and produce a runbook for testing it.\n\n## Important Details\n- Repo: `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed` (Go module `github.com/entireio/entire-agent-zed-parser`); HEAD commit `5427f10`.\n- Installed binaries: `~/.local/bin/entire` (CLI 0.9.0, Go 1.26.4), `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed` (824k? 8.2MB, built Aug 7 22:25 via `make install`), plus `entire-patched` symlink and `git-remote-entire`.\n- Reproduced both reported bugs.\n- External agent protocol (CLI v0.9.0): binaries named `entire-agent-<name>` on `$PATH`; `info` returns JSON `{\"protocol_version\":1, \"name\", \"type\", \"description\", \"is_preview\", \"protected_dirs\", \"protected_files\", \"hook_names\", \"capabilities\"}`; `detect` returns `{\"present\": bool}`; also `get-session-id`, `get-session-dir`, `resolve-session-file`, `chunk`, etc.\n- Root cause: CLI-side discovery gap. `external.Discover...` is called in `enable/setup/hooks/attach/resume` flows but NOT in `agent add`, `agent list`, or `agent remove`.\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go` `newAgentAddCmd`: calls `agent.Get(name)` directly, never discovers external agents.\n  - `runAgentList`: uses `agent.StringList()` alone, no discovery.\n  - `runRemoveAgent` (setup.go:1556): same direct `agent.Get` gap.\n  - `entire enable --agent zed` works because setup.go:893 runs `external.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways` before `agent.Get` (setup.go:902).\n- Plugin status: `info` is protocol-compliant; `detect` returns `{}` (almost false) and the plugin has no `detect` subcommand (default case prints `{}`); `are-hooks-installed` returns `{\"installed\":false}`.\n- Repo `.entire/settings.json`: `{\"enabled\":true,\"telemetry\":true,\"external_agents\":true}`; `.gitignore` for `.entire`.\n- In-repo git hooks, installed Aug 7 22:28: `commit-msg`, `post-commit`, `post-rewrite`, `pre-push`, `prepare-commit-msg` — generic Entire hooks (`entire hooks git post-commit`). The zed-specific `# --- Entire Zed Agent Lifecycle Hook ---` block from `handleInstallHooks` is NOT present in `post-commit`, so `entire enable --agent zed` did NOT install the zed lifecycle hook.\n- `entire hooks zed <event>` works via `hooks_cmd.go` fallback `RunE` → `external.DiscoverAndRegister` with 5s timeout → `executeAgentHook`.\n- Derived CLI source: cloned `entireio/cli` tag v0.9.0 (commit `8b77ad4`) to `/tmp/opencode/service-whatever` (path may change).\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Root cause located and reproducible.\n- Confirmed fix would require patching the CLI (`agent_group.go`, `setup.go`) and/or making the plugin fully protocol-compliant (add `detect`).\n- Confirmed plugin `info` output (`name:\"zed\"`, `protocol_version:1`, `type:\"Zed\"`) parses correctly.\n- Verified `entire hooks zed <event>` dispatch path exists.\n- Checked `.entire/` logs/metadata (`zed-current/`, `ses_...` entries, `pre-prompt-zed-current.json`) confirm the plugin's transcript capture worked in the past.\n\n### Active\n- Trying to decide whether to patch and rebuild the CLI locally or only make plugin-side improvements (open question from prior steps).\n- Checking `.opencode/` contents, `.entire` metadata, and `AGENTS.md` presence in repo (AGENTS.md not found).\n\n### Blocked\n- The `agent add`/`agent list` recognition failures are CLI bugs; plugin-only changes cannot make those commands discover external agents.\n- Building the CLI requires Go toolchain ≥1.26.4 (`go.mod` says `go 1.26.4`); local `go` is `go1.26.0` — may need `GOTOOLCHAIN=auto` download.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Patch `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`: in `newAgentAddCmd`, call `external.DiscoverAndRegisterNamedAlways(ctx, name)` (or `DiscoverAndRegisterAlways`) before `agent.Get`; in `runAgentList`, call `external.DiscoverAndRegister(ctx)` before printing; also patch `runRemoveAgent` in `setup.go` for symmetry.\n2. Build the patched CLI (`cd /tmp/whole-cli && go build ./cmd/entire`; resolve go toolchain), back up `~/.local/bin/entire`, install, re-test `entire agent list` and `entire agent add zed`.\n3. Add a `detect` subcommand to `entire-agent-zed/main.go` returning `{\"present\": true}` (or true when Zed DB is available), then re-run `make install`.\n4. Verify the zed lifecycle hook: run `entire enable --agent zed` (or `entire-agent-zed install-hooks`), confirm `.git/hooks/post-commit` contains `# Entire Zed Agent lifecycle hook`, then run a test commit and examine `.entire/logs/entire.log` for zed `turn-start`/`turn-end` events.\n5. Write a testing runbook (e.g., `docs/HookTesting.md` or README section) documenting: setup flow, expected hook output, how to inspect `.entire/metadata/zed-…/full.jsonl`, and how to confirm now a valid Zed transcript/checkpoint is created.\n\n## Relevant Files:\n- `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/model-entire-agent-zed/main.go` (plugin subcommand handlers; add `detect`)\n- `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/model-entire-agent-zed/Makefile` (`make install` → `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed`)\n- `/tmp/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go` (CLI `newAgentAddCmd`/`newAgentListCmd` fix location)\n- `/tmp/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/setup.go` (lines 868-902 external discovery before `agent.Get`; line 1556 `runRemoveAgent` gap)\n- `/tmp/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/{discovery,types,capabilities}.go` (protocol definitions)\n- `/tmp/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go` and `hook_registry.go` (hook dispatch for `entire hooks zed session-start` etc.)\n- `.entire/settings.json` (contains `external_agents: true`)\n- `.git/hooks/post-commit` (currently lacks the zed lifecycle marker; target for fix)\n- `~/.local/bin/entire` (installed CLI 0.9.0 to be rebuilt/reinstalled if CLI fix is applied)",
