            },
            "output": "### info\n\nSource: https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md\n\nReturns agent metadata and declared capabilities. This is a required subcommand for agent discovery.\n\n```APIDOC\n## info\n\n### Description\nReturns agent metadata and declared capabilities. This is a required subcommand for agent discovery.\n\n### Method\nNot applicable (subcommand-based protocol)\n\n### Endpoint\nNot applicable (subcommand-based protocol)\n\n### Parameters\n#### Path Parameters\nNone\n\n#### Query Parameters\nNone\n\n#### Request Body\nNone\n\n### Request Example\nNone\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response (stdout)\n- **protocol_version** (integer) - The protocol version implemented by the agent.\n- **name** (string) - The name of the agent.\n- **type** (string) - The type of the agent.\n- **description** (string) - A brief description of the agent.\n- **is_preview** (boolean) - Indicates if the agent is in preview.\n- **protected_dirs** (array of strings) - Directories that should not be modified by the agent.\n- **hook_names** (array of strings) - Names of hooks the agent supports.\n- **capabilities** (object) - An object detailing the agent's capabilities.\n  - **hooks** (boolean) - Whether the agent supports hooks.\n  - **transcript_analyzer** (boolean) - Whether the agent can analyze transcripts.\n  - **transcript_preparer** (boolean) - Whether the agent can prepare transcripts.\n  - **token_calculator** (boolean) - Whether the agent can calculate tokens.\n  - **text_generator** (boolean) - Whether the agent can generate text.\n  - **hook_response_writer** (boolean) - Whether the agent can write hook responses.\n  - **subagent_aware_extractor** (boolean) - Whether the agent is aware of subagents.\n\n#### Response Example\n```json\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"cursor\",\n  \"type\": \"Cursor\",\n  \"description\": \"Cursor - AI-powered code editor\",\n  \"is_preview\": true,\n  \"protected_dirs\": [\".cursor\"],\n  \"hook_names\": [\"session-start\", \"session-end\", \"stop\"],\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"hooks\": true,\n    \"transcript_analyzer\": true,\n    \"transcript_preparer\": false,\n    \"token_calculator\": false,\n    \"text_generator\": false,\n    \"hook_response_writer\": false,\n    \"subagent_aware_extractor\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### detect\n\nSource: https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md\n\nChecks whether the agent is present and usable in the current environment. This is a required subcommand.\n\n```APIDOC\n## detect\n\n### Description\nChecks whether the agent is present and usable in the current environment. This is a required subcommand.\n\n### Method\nNot applicable (subcommand-based protocol)\n\n### Endpoint\nNot applicable (subcommand-based protocol)\n\n### Parameters\n#### Path Parameters\nNone\n\n#### Query Parameters\nNone\n\n#### Request Body\nNone\n\n### Request Example\nNone\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response (stdout)\n- **present** (boolean) - True if the agent is present and usable, false otherwise.\n\n#### Response Example\n```json\n{\"present\": true}\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Define Agent Hook Names and Event Parsing Logic\n\nSource: https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/agent-guide.md\n\nImplement the HookNames and ParseHookEvent methods for an agent. This function defines the supported hook names and handles the parsing of different event types from standard input.\n\n```go\npackage youragent\n\nimport (\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tHookNameSessionStart = \"session-start\"\n\tHookNameSessionEnd   = \"session-end\"\n\tHookNamePromptSubmit = \"prompt-submit\"\n\tHookNameResponse     = \"response\"\n)\n\nfunc (a *YourAgent) HookNames() []string {\n\treturn []string{\n\t\tHookNameSessionStart,\n\t\tHookNameSessionEnd,\n\t\tHookNamePromptSubmit,\n\t\tHookNameResponse,\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (a *YourAgent) ParseHookEvent(hookName string, stdin io.Reader) (*agent.Event, error) {\n\tswitch hookName {\n\tcase HookNameSessionStart:\n\t\traw, err := agent.ReadAndParseHookInput[sessionInfoRaw](stdin)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn &agent.Event{\n\t\t\tType:       agent.SessionStart,\n\t\t\tSessionID:  raw.SessionID,\n\t\t\tSessionRef: raw.TranscriptPath,\n\t\t\tTimestamp:  time.Now(),\n\t\t},\n\t\tnil\n\n\tcase HookNamePromptSubmit:\n\t\traw, err := agent.ReadAndParseHookInput[promptInputRaw](stdin)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn &agent.Event{\n\t\t\tType:       agent.TurnStart,\n\t\t\tSessionID:  raw.SessionID,\n\t\t\tSessionRef: raw.TranscriptPath,\n\t\t\tPrompt:     raw.Prompt,\n\t\t\tTimestamp:  time.Now(),\n\t\t},\n\t\tnil\n\n\tcase HookNameResponse:\n\t\traw, err := agent.ReadAndParseHookInput[sessionInfoRaw](stdin)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn &agent.Event{\n\t\t\tType:       agent.TurnEnd,\n\t\t\tSessionID:  raw.SessionID,\n\t\t\tSessionRef: raw.TranscriptPath,\n\t\t\tTimestamp:  time.Now(),\n\t\t},\n\t\tnil\n\n\tcase HookNameSessionEnd:\n\t\traw, err := agent.ReadAndParseHookInput[sessionInfoRaw](stdin)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn &agent.Event{\n\t\t\tType:       agent.SessionEnd,\n\t\t\tSessionID:  raw.SessionID,\n\t\t\tSessionRef: raw.TranscriptPath,\n\t\t\tTimestamp:  time.Now(),\n\t\t},\n\t\tnil\n\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn nil, nil //nolint:nilnil // nil event = no lifecycle action\n\t}\n}\n\n```\n\n### External Agent Plugin Protocol > Discovery\n\nSource: https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md\n\nThe CLI discovers external agents by searching the system's PATH for executables named `entire-agent-<name>`. For example, `entire-agent-cursor` would be registered as the 'cursor' agent. Agents with names that conflict with built-in agents are skipped. Discovery occurs once during CLI initialization, and the agent binary must be executable and respond to the `info` subcommand.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### External Agent Protocol > Versioning\n\nSource: https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md\n\nThe protocol version is determined by the 'protocol_version' field in the 'info' response and the 'ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION' environment variable. The CLI verifies that the agent's protocol version aligns with its expected version before registration. Future protocol versions might introduce new subcommands or features, but existing subcommands will remain backward compatible within a major version.",
