            "output": "<path>/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # External Agent Plugin Protocol\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: The Entire CLI supports external agent plugins — standalone binaries that implement the Agent interface via a subcommand-based protocol over stdin/stdout. This allows third-party agents to integrate with the CLI without modifying the main repository.\n6: \n7: ## Discovery\n8: \n9: The CLI discovers external agents by scanning `$PATH` for executables matching the pattern `entire-agent-<name>`. For example, `entire-agent-cursor` would register as the \"cursor\" agent.\n10: \n11: - Binaries whose `<name>` conflicts with an already-registered built-in agent are skipped.\n12: - Discovery runs once during CLI initialization (before building the hooks command tree).\n13: - The binary must be executable and respond to the `info` subcommand.\n14: \n15: ## Environment\n16: \n17: Every subcommand invocation sets:\n18: \n19: | Variable | Description |\n20: |---|---|\n21: | `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` | Absolute path to the git repository root |\n22: | `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` | Protocol version (`1`) |\n23: \n24: The working directory is set to the repository root.\n25: \n26: ## Communication Model\n27: \n28: - **Subcommand-based:** Each Agent interface method maps to a CLI subcommand.\n29: - **JSON over stdin/stdout:** Structured data uses JSON. Transcripts use raw bytes.\n30: - **Stateless:** Each invocation is independent — no persistent connection.\n31: - **Exit codes:** `0` = success, non-zero = error. Error messages go to stderr.\n32: \n33: ## Subcommands\n34: \n35: ### Always Required\n36: \n37: #### `info`\n38: \n39: Returns agent metadata and declared capabilities.\n40: \n41: **Arguments:** None\n42: \n43: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n44: \n45: ```json\n46: {\n47:   \"protocol_version\": 1,\n48:   \"name\": \"cursor\",\n49:   \"type\": \"Cursor\",\n50:   \"description\": \"Cursor - AI-powered code editor\",\n51:   \"is_preview\": true,\n52:   \"protected_dirs\": [\".cursor\"],\n53:   \"hook_names\": [\"session-start\", \"session-end\", \"stop\"],\n54:   \"capabilities\": {\n55:     \"hooks\": true,\n56:     \"transcript_analyzer\": true,\n57:     \"transcript_preparer\": false,\n58:     \"token_calculator\": false,\n59:     \"text_generator\": false,\n60:     \"hook_response_writer\": false,\n61:     \"subagent_aware_extractor\": false\n62:   }\n63: }\n64: ```\n65: \n66: The `capabilities` object determines which optional subcommands the CLI will call. If a capability is `false` or missing, the CLI will never invoke the corresponding subcommands.\n67: \n68: #### `detect`\n69: \n70: Checks whether the agent is present/usable in the current environment.\n71: \n72: **Arguments:** None\n73: \n74: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n75: \n76: ```json\n77: {\"present\": true}\n78: ```\n79: \n80: #### `get-session-id`\n81: \n82: Extracts the session ID from a hook input event.\n83: \n84: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n85: \n86: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n87: \n88: ```json\n89: {\"session_id\": \"abc123\"}\n90: ```\n91: \n92: #### `get-session-dir --repo-path <path>`\n93: \n94: Returns the directory where agent sessions are stored.\n95: \n96: **Arguments:**\n97: - `--repo-path` — Absolute path to the repository\n98: \n99: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n100: \n101: ```json\n102: {\"session_dir\": \"/path/to/sessions\"}\n103: ```\n104: \n105: #### `resolve-session-file --session-dir <dir> --session-id <id>`\n106: \n107: Resolves the session file path from a session directory and ID.\n108: \n109: **Arguments:**\n110: - `--session-dir` — Session directory path\n111: - `--session-id` — Session identifier\n112: \n113: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n114: \n115: ```json\n116: {\"session_file\": \"/path/to/session/file.jsonl\"}\n117: ```\n118: \n119: #### `read-session`\n120: \n121: Reads session data from a hook input event.\n122: \n123: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [HookInput object](#hookinput-object)\n124: \n125: **Output (stdout):** JSON — [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n126: \n127: ```json\n128: {\n129:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n130:   \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n131:   \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n132:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/file.jsonl\",\n133:   \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n134:   \"native_data\": null,\n135:   \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n136:   \"new_files\": [],\n137:   \"deleted_files\": []\n138: }\n139: ```\n140: \n141: #### `write-session`\n142: \n143: Writes/updates session data.\n144: \n145: **Input (stdin):** JSON — the [AgentSession object](#agentsession-object)\n146: \n147: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n148: \n149: #### `read-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n150: \n151: Reads a transcript file and returns its raw bytes.\n152: \n153: **Arguments:**\n154: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n155: \n156: **Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n157: \n158: #### `chunk-transcript --max-size <n>`\n159: \n160: Splits a transcript into chunks for storage.\n161: \n162: **Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n163: \n164: **Arguments:**\n165: - `--max-size` — Maximum chunk size in bytes\n166: \n167: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n168: \n169: ```json\n170: {\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n171: ```\n172: \n173: #### `reassemble-transcript`\n174: \n175: Reassembles transcript chunks back into a full transcript.\n176: \n177: **Input (stdin):** JSON\n178: \n179: ```json\n180: {\"chunks\": [\"<base64-encoded-chunk>\", \"...\"]}\n181: ```\n182: \n183: **Output (stdout):** Raw transcript bytes.\n184: \n185: #### `format-resume-command --session-id <id>`\n186: \n187: Returns the command a user can run to resume a session.\n188: \n189: **Arguments:**\n190: - `--session-id` — Session identifier\n191: \n192: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n193: \n194: ```json\n195: {\"command\": \"cursor --resume abc123\"}\n196: ```\n197: \n198: ### Capability: `hooks`\n199: \n200: These subcommands are required when `capabilities.hooks` is `true`.\n201: \n202: #### `parse-hook --hook <name>`\n203: \n204: Parses a raw agent hook payload into a structured event.\n205: \n206: **Arguments:**\n207: - `--hook` — Hook name (e.g., \"stop\", \"session-start\")\n208: \n209: **Input (stdin):** Raw agent hook payload bytes.\n210: \n211: **Output (stdout):** JSON — the parsed [Event object](#event-object), or `null` if the payload is not relevant.\n212: \n213: #### `install-hooks [--local-dev] [--force]`\n214: \n215: Installs agent hooks for Entire integration.\n216: \n217: **Arguments:**\n218: - `--local-dev` — Use local development binary path (optional)\n219: - `--force` — Overwrite existing hooks (optional)\n220: \n221: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n222: \n223: ```json\n224: {\"hooks_installed\": 3}\n225: ```\n226: \n227: #### `uninstall-hooks`\n228: \n229: Removes installed agent hooks.\n230: \n231: **Arguments:** None\n232: \n233: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n234: \n235: #### `are-hooks-installed`\n236: \n237: Checks whether hooks are currently installed.\n238: \n239: **Arguments:** None\n240: \n241: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n242: \n243: ```json\n244: {\"installed\": true}\n245: ```\n246: \n247: ### Capability: `transcript_analyzer`\n248: \n249: Required when `capabilities.transcript_analyzer` is `true`.\n250: \n251: #### `get-transcript-position --path <path>`\n252: \n253: Returns the current byte position/size of a transcript file.\n254: \n255: **Arguments:**\n256: - `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n257: \n258: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n259: \n260: ```json\n261: {\"position\": 12345}\n262: ```\n263: \n264: #### `extract-modified-files --path <path> --offset <n>`\n265: \n266: Extracts the list of files modified by the agent from a transcript.\n267: \n268: **Arguments:**\n269: - `--path` — Path to the transcript file\n270: - `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n271: \n272: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n273: \n274: ```json\n275: {\"files\": [\"path/to/file1.go\", \"path/to/file2.go\"], \"current_position\": 12345}\n276: ```\n277: \n278: The `current_position` field returns the transcript position after extraction, allowing the caller to resume from that point on subsequent calls.\n279: \n280: #### `extract-prompts --session-ref <path> --offset <n>`\n281: \n282: Extracts user prompts from a transcript.\n283: \n284: **Arguments:**\n285: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n286: - `--offset` — Byte offset to start reading from\n287: \n288: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n289: \n290: ```json\n291: {\"prompts\": [\"first prompt text\", \"second prompt text\"]}\n292: ```\n293: \n294: #### `extract-summary --session-ref <path>`\n295: \n296: Extracts an AI-generated summary from a transcript.\n297: \n298: **Arguments:**\n299: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n300: \n301: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n302: \n303: ```json\n304: {\"summary\": \"Summary text here\", \"has_summary\": true}\n305: ```\n306: \n307: ### Capability: `transcript_preparer`\n308: \n309: Required when `capabilities.transcript_preparer` is `true`.\n310: \n311: #### `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>`\n312: \n313: Prepares/processes a transcript file (e.g., converting from raw format).\n314: \n315: **Arguments:**\n316: - `--session-ref` — Path to the transcript file\n317: \n318: **Output:** Exit 0 on success.\n319: \n320: ### Capability: `token_calculator`\n321: \n322: Required when `capabilities.token_calculator` is `true`.\n323: \n324: #### `calculate-tokens --offset <n>`\n325: \n326: Calculates token usage from a transcript.\n327: \n328: **Input (stdin):** Raw transcript bytes.\n329: \n330: **Arguments:**\n331: - `--offset` — Byte offset to start calculating from\n332: \n333: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n334: \n335: ```json\n336: {\n337:   \"input_tokens\": 1500,\n338:   \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n339:   \"cache_read_tokens\": 200,\n340:   \"output_tokens\": 500,\n341:   \"api_call_count\": 3,\n342:   \"subagent_tokens\": null\n343: }\n344: ```\n345: \n346: Only `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` are required. The optional fields (`cache_creation_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `api_call_count`) default to `0` if omitted. `subagent_tokens` is an optional nested object with the same structure, for agents that spawn subagents.\n347: \n348: ### Capability: `text_generator`\n349: \n350: Required when `capabilities.text_generator` is `true`.\n351: \n352: External agents that declare `capabilities.text_generator: true` can be used as\n353: summary providers for `entire explain --generate` and checkpoint auto-summarize.\n354: Configure them with:\n355: \n356: ```bash\n357: entire configure --summarize-provider <agent-name> [--summarize-model <model>]\n358: ```\n359: \n360: The provider name is derived from the executable name `entire-agent-<agent-name>`.\n361: The CLI passes Entire's summary prompt on stdin to `generate-text --model <model>`\n362: and expects `{\"text\":\"...\"}` on stdout.\n363: \n364: #### `generate-text --model <model>`\n365: \n366: Generates text using the agent's underlying LLM.\n367: \n368: **Input (stdin):** Prompt text.\n369: \n370: **Arguments:**\n371: - `--model` — Model to use for generation\n372: \n373: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n374: \n375: ```json\n376: {\"text\": \"Generated response text\"}\n377: ```\n378: \n379: ### Capability: `hook_response_writer`\n380: \n381: Required when `capabilities.hook_response_writer` is `true`.\n382: \n383: #### `write-hook-response --message <message>`\n384: \n385: Writes a message in the agent's native hook response format.\n386: \n387: **Arguments:**\n388: - `--message` — Message to write\n389: \n390: **Output (stdout):** Agent-native format bytes (e.g., JSONL for Claude Code).\n391: \n392: ### Capability: `subagent_aware_extractor`\n393: \n394: Required when `capabilities.subagent_aware_extractor` is `true`.\n395: \n396: #### `extract-all-modified-files --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n397: \n398: Extracts modified files from both the main transcript and any subagent transcripts.\n399: \n400: **Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n401: \n402: **Arguments:**\n403: - `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n404: - `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n405: \n406: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n407: \n408: ```json\n409: {\"files\": [\"file1.go\", \"file2.go\"]}\n410: ```\n411: \n412: #### `calculate-total-tokens --offset <n> --subagents-dir <dir>`\n413: \n414: Calculates total token usage across main transcript and subagent transcripts.\n415: \n416: **Input (stdin):** Raw main transcript bytes.\n417: \n418: **Arguments:**\n419: - `--offset` — Byte offset for the main transcript\n420: - `--subagents-dir` — Directory containing subagent transcripts\n421: \n422: **Output (stdout):** JSON\n423: \n424: ```json\n425: {\n426:   \"input_tokens\": 5000,\n427:   \"cache_creation_tokens\": 0,\n428:   \"cache_read_tokens\": 1000,\n429:   \"output_tokens\": 2000,\n430:   \"api_call_count\": 8,\n431:   \"subagent_tokens\": {\n432:     \"input_tokens\": 2000,\n433:     \"output_tokens\": 800\n434:   }\n435: }\n436: ```\n437: \n438: Same token usage format as `calculate-tokens`. The `subagent_tokens` field aggregates usage from all subagents.\n439: \n440: ## Shared Object Definitions\n441: \n442: ### HookInput Object\n443: \n444: The HookInput object is passed via stdin to `get-session-id` and `read-session`.\n445: \n446: ```json\n447: {\n448:   \"hook_type\": \"stop\",\n449:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n450:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n451:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n452:   \"user_prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n453:   \"tool_name\": \"Write\",\n454:   \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_abc123\",\n455:   \"tool_input\": {\"path\": \"/src/main.go\"},\n456:   \"raw_data\": {\"custom_field\": \"value\"}\n457: }\n458: ```\n459: \n460: | Field | Type | Description |\n461: |---|---|---|\n462: | `hook_type` | string | Hook type: `session_start`, `session_end`, `user_prompt_submit`, `stop`, `pre_tool_use`, `post_tool_use` |\n463: | `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n464: | `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific session reference (typically a file path) |\n465: | `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp |\n466: | `user_prompt` | string | User's prompt text (from `user_prompt_submit` hooks). Optional. |\n467: | `tool_name` | string | Tool name (from `pre_tool_use`/`post_tool_use` hooks). Optional. |\n468: | `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID. Optional. |\n469: | `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON. Optional. |\n470: | `raw_data` | object | Agent-specific data for extension. Optional. |\n471: \n472: ### AgentSession Object\n473: \n474: Used as input to `write-session` and output from `read-session`.\n475: \n476: ```json\n477: {\n478:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n479:   \"agent_name\": \"cursor\",\n480:   \"repo_path\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n481:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n482:   \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\",\n483:   \"native_data\": null,\n484:   \"modified_files\": [\"src/main.go\"],\n485:   \"new_files\": [\"src/new_file.go\"],\n486:   \"deleted_files\": []\n487: }\n488: ```\n489: \n490: | Field | Type | Description |\n491: |---|---|---|\n492: | `session_id` | string | Agent session identifier |\n493: | `agent_name` | string | Agent registry name |\n494: | `repo_path` | string | Absolute path to the repository |\n495: | `session_ref` | string | Path/reference to session in agent's storage |\n496: | `start_time` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp of session start |\n497: | `native_data` | bytes/null | Session content in agent's native format (opaque to CLI) |\n498: | `modified_files` | string[] | Files modified during the session |\n499: | `new_files` | string[] | Files created during the session |\n500: | `deleted_files` | string[] | Files deleted during the session |\n501: \n502: ### Event Object\n503: \n504: Returned by `parse-hook`. Represents a normalized lifecycle event.\n505: \n506: ```json\n507: {\n508:   \"type\": 3,\n509:   \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n510:   \"session_ref\": \"/path/to/transcript.jsonl\",\n511:   \"prompt\": \"Fix the login bug\",\n512:   \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n513:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-13T12:00:00Z\"\n514: }\n515: ```\n516: \n517: | Field | Type | Description |\n518: |---|---|---|\n519: | `type` | int | **Required.** Event type (see table below) |\n520: | `session_id` | string | **Required.** Agent session identifier |\n521: | `previous_session_id` | string | Non-empty when this event represents a session continuation/handoff. Optional. |\n522: | `session_ref` | string | Agent-specific transcript reference. Optional. |\n523: | `prompt` | string | User's prompt text (on `TurnStart` events). Optional. |\n524: | `model` | string | LLM model identifier. Optional. |\n525: | `timestamp` | string | RFC 3339 timestamp. Optional. |\n526: | `tool_use_id` | string | Tool invocation ID (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n527: | `subagent_id` | string | Subagent instance ID (for `SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n528: | `tool_input` | object | Raw tool input JSON (for subagent type/description extraction). Optional. |\n529: | `subagent_type` | string | Kind of subagent (for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`). Optional. |\n530: | `task_description` | string | Subagent task description. Optional. |\n531: | `response_message` | string | Message to display to the user via the agent. Optional. |\n532: | `metadata` | object | Agent-specific state preserved across events. Optional. |\n533: \n534: **Event types:**\n535: \n536: | Value | Name | Description |\n537: |---|---|---|\n538: | 1 | SessionStart | Agent session has begun |\n539: | 2 | TurnStart | User submitted a prompt, agent is about to work |\n540: | 3 | TurnEnd | Agent finished responding to a prompt |\n541: | 4 | Compaction | Agent is compressing its context window (triggers save + offset reset) |\n542: | 5 | SessionEnd | Session has been terminated |\n543: | 6 | SubagentStart | A subagent (task) has been spawned |\n544: | 7 | SubagentEnd | A subagent (task) has completed |\n545: \n546: ## Error Handling\n547: \n548: - Exit code `0` indicates success.\n549: - Any non-zero exit code indicates an error.\n550: - Error messages should be written to stderr.\n551: - The CLI captures stderr and wraps it in a Go error.\n552: - If the binary is not found in PATH, the agent is simply not registered.\n553: - If `info` fails or returns invalid JSON, the binary is skipped during discovery.\n554: \n555: ## Versioning\n556: \n557: The protocol version is declared in the `info` response (`protocol_version` field) and set via `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION` environment variable. The CLI checks that the binary's protocol version matches its expected version before registering the agent.\n558: \n559: Future protocol versions may add new subcommands or capabilities. Existing subcommands will maintain backwards compatibility within a major version.\n\n(End of file - total 559 lines)\n</content>",
