 If the raw data is large, that's fine. But there's a 10MB output limit. Zed threads could be large but usually under 10MB. OK.\n\nAlso, I should update the help text to mention the new protocol commands. Let me update printHelp.\n\nNow let me also double check: does the CLI's `fileExists(transcriptRef)` check pass? transcriptRef = dbPath (the DB file). The DB file exists. Good. So `prepare-transcript` no-op is fine, and `read-transcript` reads the DB.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety in lifecycle.go: `transcriptRef := event.SessionRef`. The plugin's parse-hook returns `session_ref = dbPath`. So transcriptRef = dbPath. fileExists(dbPath) = true. Good.\n\nThen `ag.ReadTranscript(transcriptRef)` → `read-transcript --session-ref <dbPath>` → returns raw thread bytes. Good.\n\nThen `ExtractPrompts(transcriptRef, offset)` → `extract-prompts --session-ref <dbPath> --offset <n>`. Good.\n\nThen `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset(transcriptRef, offset)` → `extract-modified-files --path <dbPath> --offset <n>`. Good.\n\nThen `CalculateTokenUsage(transcriptData, offset)` → `calculate-tokens` with transcriptData on stdin. Good.\n\nSo the flow works with the DB path as session_ref. \n\nNow let me implement. First, add strconv import. Then update the switch. Then update handleInfo. Then add the new handlers.\n\nLet me make the edits.",
