          "text": "## Objective\n- Diagnose why `entire` CLI 0.9.0 does not recognize the `entire-agent-zed` plugin (`entire agent add zed` errors `unknown agent \"zed\"`; `agent list` omits Zed).\n- Per user direction (no CLI patching first): fix `entire-agent-zed` to the external-agent protocol spec, re-test; if it works but is unlisted, file/update an Entire bug issue; only if still broken while compliant, craft a CLI patch and submit with the issue. Also verify the zed git hook fires and write a test runbook.\n\n## Important Details\n- Repo: `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed` (Go module `github.com/entireio/entire-agent-zed-parser`); installed binaries `~/.local/bin/entire` (0.9.0) and `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed` (STILL STALE — `make install` not yet run after code changes); plus `entire-patched` symlink and `git-remote-entire`.\n- CLI source: `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli` (unshallowed, 7094 commits; tag v0.9.0 == commit `8b77ad4`); builds cleanly with GOTOOLCHAIN=auto (go1.26.4).\n- User decision: do NOT patch the CLI yet; compliance-first plan. CLI archaeology unchanged: `agent add/list/remove` introduced in `c4109895` and NEVER discover externals; `detect`/`hook_names` required since initial commit `74114ec2`; no global discovery (per-command only).\n- Plugin now implements ALL protocol subcommands (implemented this session): `detect`, `get-session-id`, `read-session`, `write-session`, `read-transcript`, `chunk-transcript`, `reassemble-transcript`, `format-resume-command`, `get-transcript-position`, `extract-modified-files`, `extract-prompts`, `extract-summary`, `prepare-transcript`; `handleInfo` now includes `hook_names: [\"session-start\",\"turn-start\",\"turn-end\",\"session-end\"]`. Capabilities kept as declared (`transcript_analyzer`, `transcript_preparer`, `hooks`, `token_calculator`) — all required subcommands now exist, so declaration is honest.\n- Key lifecycle resolution: `session_ref` from `parse-hook` is the Zed DB path; the DB is a real file, so the `fileExists(transcriptRef)` gate (lifecycle.go:684-695) passes; `read-transcript --session-ref <dbPath>` now returns raw decompressed thread data, which the CLI writes as the transcript file. `extract-prompts`/`extract-modified-files`/`extract-summary` read the DB at `--session-ref`/`--path`.\n- Degraded-but-functional caveat: `handleCalculateTokens` still reads the DB directly and ignores stdin + `--offset` (the CLI pipes transcript data into `calculate-tokens --offset N`); token counts may reflect the full session rather than the offset delta.\n- CLI invoke shapes confirmed from `external/external.go` + `external/types.go`: `chunk-transcript --max-size N` (content on stdin) returns base64 `chunks` (`ChunkResponse.Chunks [][]byte`); `read-transcript` returns raw bytes; failures output `{}` exit 0 (non-fatal — e.g. `ReadTranscript` yields `[]byte(\"{}\")`).\n- `format-resume-command` returns `{\"command\":\"\"}` (Zed has no CLI resume command) — acceptable.\n- Host has real Zed data: `detect` → `{\"present\":true}`; `read-session` returns base64 `native_data` of latest thread (\"Updating Lemonade LXC Root Keys\").\n- `.git/hooks/post-commit` in zed repo still lacks the \"Entire Zed Agent Lifecycle Hook\" block that install-hooks writes — still unresolved why `entire enable --agent zed` didn't leave it.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Reproduced both bugs; CLI artifact inventory; unshallowed CLI repo + archaeology (noun-group never had discovery; detect/hook_names required since protocol inception).\n- Completed plugin-vs-spec audit; read external types/discovery/capabilities, registry, hooks_cmd.go, lifecycle.go, setup.go hook flow, plugin main.go handlers.\n- Applied then REVERTED trial CLI patch to `agent_group.go` per user decision; CLI repo clean.\n- Implemented plugin compliance fixes in `main.go`: added `strconv` import; new switch cases (lines ~141-190); `handleInfo` with `hook_names`; new handlers + helpers (`flagValue`, `flagInt`, `readStdin`, `openDBFromRef`, `fetchRawFromRef`, `extractFilePathsFromTool`); fixed `rawTime`→`rawData` typo in `handleReadSession`.\n- Build clean: `go build -o /tmp/opencode/entire-agent-zed-test .` exit 0.\n- Manual verification of all new subcommands passed (info shows hook_names, detect present:true, chunk↔reassemble round-trip \"hello world\", get-transcript-position returns file size, missing-DB paths return non-fatal `{}`/empty arrays).\n- Full existing suite passes: `go test -count=1 ./...` → ok (18.888s).\n- Added 14 new binary tests in `main_test.go` (after `TestBinary_Stop`, ~line 356; added `bytes` import), following `buildBinary` conventions; all pass (12.064s run).\n\n### Active\n- `make install` NOT yet run — `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed` is still the OLD binary; new code only at `/tmp/opencode/entire-agent-zed-test`.\n- Todo list: audit completed; \"fix plugin\" code + tests done, install pending; enable/commit verification pending.\n\n### Blocked\n- `agent add/list/remove` recognition remains a CLI-side discovery gap; per user plan this becomes a filed bug issue, not a local patch.\n- Unresolved: why `entire enable --agent zed` did not leave the zed lifecycle hook block in `.git/hooks/post-commit`.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Run `make install` in `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed` to rebuild `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed` with the new protocol subcommands.\n2. Re-test: `entire enable --agent zed`, then make a test commit; verify `.git/hooks/post-commit` contains the \"Entire Zed Agent Lifecycle Hook\" block and `.entire/logs/entire.log` shows zed `turn-start`/`turn-end`/checkpoint events; inspect `.entire/metadata/zed-…/full.jsonl` (transcript should now be populated, not `{}`).\n3. Decide outcome per user plan: works-but-unlisted → file/update the Entire bug issue for `agent add/list` discovery; still broken while compliant → craft the CLI patch (`agent_group.go` add/list + `setup.go:1556` remove) and submit with the issue.\n4. Write the hook-testing runbook (e.g., `docs/HookTesting.md` or README section).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed/main.go`: subcommand switch ~141-190; `handleInfo` ~235 (now with hook_names); `getZedDBPath` 817; `handleParseHook` 894 (returns DB path as session_ref); `handleResolveSessionFile` ~1585; new protocol handlers inserted after it (~1596+; `handleReadSession` ~1733); `handleInstallHooks`/`handleCalculateTokens` shifted down ~350 lines from their old 1618/1742 positions.\n- `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed/main_test.go`: `buildBinary` 311; `TestBinary_Info` 323; 14 new subcommand tests after `TestBinary_Stop` (~356+).\n- `/home/brian/mule_dev/R/entire-agent-zed/Makefile`: `make install` → `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed` (NOT yet run since code change).\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli`: CLI repo (v0.9.0 = 8b77ad4); clean working tree.\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md`: spec.\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`: noun-group discovery gap (introduced `c4109895`).\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`: `setupAgentHooks` 1637; `DiscoverAndRegisterAlways` 893; `runRemoveAgent` 1556.\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/{external,types}.go`: invoke shapes + response types (`DetectResponse`, `SessionIDResponse`, base64 `ChunkResponse`).\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`: 684-695 fileExists gate; 749-780 ExtractPrompts prompt.txt backfill.\n- `/tmp/opencode/entireio-cli/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go` + `hook_registry.go`: `entire hooks zed <event>` RunE fallback via `executeAgentHook`.\n- `.git/hooks/post-commit` in zed repo: still lacks lifecycle block; target for verification.\n- `~/.local/bin/entire`, `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-zed`: installed binaries (plugin binary stale until `make install`).",
