          "type": "text",
          "text": "Wrote `HANDOFF.md` at the repo root. It covers:\n\n- **State**: plugin is protocol-compliant, all subcommands implemented, tests pass, `make install` done.\n- **What works**: `entire hooks zed <event>` fires lifecycle events; checkpoints write.\n- **What's broken**: `agent add/list` never discover external agents — a CLI-side bug (`agent_group.go`, since `c4109895`), not a plugin issue. Per your decision, report upstream, don't patch locally.\n- **Gotchas**: the `{}` transcript is correct (no Zed thread for this repo yet); the post-commit hook is wired via chaining to `post-commit.pre-entire`, not inline.\n- **Next steps**: start a real Zed session, commit, verify log + `full.jsonl`, then file the CLI bug.\n\nOne thing to double-check: you said \"continue integration testing of your fixes\" — the doc assumes the Zed agent will run a real session in this repo. If you'd rather it test in a scratch repo, adjust step 1. Otherwise it's ready.",
